<style>
    /* ==============================
   Case Studies List
============================== */

.case-studies-list-section {
    padding: 64px 0;
}

.case-studies-list-container {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
}

.case-studies-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
    background: #e5e5e5;
}

.case-study-card {
    background: #ffffff;
    padding: 40px;
}

.case-study-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px 24px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    color: #737373;
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
}

.case-study-meta-primary {
    color: #000000;
}

.case-study-title {
    max-width: 24ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #171717;
    font-size: 30px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
}

.case-study-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 40px;
    margin-top: 32px;
}

.case-study-column {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
}

.case-study-block h3 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: #737373;
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
}

.case-study-block p {
    margin: 0;
    color: rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.9);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
}

.case-study-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
}

.case-study-list li {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    color: rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.9);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
}

.case-study-list li::before {
    content: "";
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 16px;
    height: 1px;
    margin-top: 11px;
    background: #000000;
}


/* ==============================
   Responsive
============================== */

@media (max-width: 767px) {
    .case-studies-list-section {
        padding: 48px 0;
    }

    .case-studies-list-container {
        padding: 0 20px;
    }

    .case-study-card {
        padding: 28px 24px;
    }

    .case-study-meta {
        gap: 8px 16px;
    }

    .case-study-title {
        font-size: 26px;
    }

    .case-study-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 32px;
        margin-top: 28px;
    }

    .case-study-column {
        gap: 24px;
    }
}
</style>

<section class="case-studies-list-section">
    <div class="case-studies-list-container">

        <div class="case-studies-list">

            <!-- Store 01 -->
            <article class="case-study-card">
                <div class="case-study-meta">
                    <span class="case-study-meta-primary">Store 01</span>
                    <span>Focus: Conversion Rate Optimization</span>
                    <span>Stage: Existing store</span>
                </div>

                <h2 class="case-study-title">
                    Traffic arrives, but the checkout journey leaks
                </h2>

                <div class="case-study-grid">

                    <div class="case-study-column">

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Challenge</h3>
                            <p>
                                A store is paying for traffic and getting visits,
                                but a large share of sessions end on the product
                                page or in the cart without an order being placed.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Store situation</h3>
                            <p>
                                Product pages carry thin copy and unclear shipping
                                information, the cart requires several taps to reach
                                checkout on mobile, and trust signals appear only
                                after payment details are requested.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Strategy</h3>
                            <p>
                                Work the funnel in the order money is lost:
                                product page clarity first, then cart and checkout
                                friction, then post-purchase reassurance. Change
                                one thing at a time so the effect of each change
                                stays readable.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                    <div class="case-study-column">

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Implementation</h3>

                            <ul class="case-study-list">
                                <li>
                                    Rewrite product page structure: price, variant,
                                    shipping and returns visible without scrolling
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Reduce cart-to-checkout steps and enable express
                                    payment options
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Add returns, delivery and support information
                                    above the fold on mobile
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Track add-to-cart, checkout-start and purchase
                                    separately to find the real drop point
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>What this is designed to change</h3>

                            <ul class="case-study-list">
                                <li>
                                    Fewer sessions abandoned at product-page level
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    A shorter, clearer path from cart to payment
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    A measurable baseline so future changes can be
                                    judged, not guessed
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>
            </article>


            <!-- Store 02 -->
            <article class="case-study-card">
                <div class="case-study-meta">
                    <span class="case-study-meta-primary">Store 02</span>
                    <span>Focus: Store Redesign</span>
                    <span>Stage: Rebuild</span>
                </div>

                <h2 class="case-study-title">
                    A store that grew feature by feature and lost its shape
                </h2>

                <div class="case-study-grid">

                    <div class="case-study-column">

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Challenge</h3>
                            <p>
                                A store has been edited for two years by different
                                hands. Navigation has grown to a long list,
                                collections overlap, and the theme is slowed by
                                apps that are no longer used.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Store situation</h3>
                            <p>
                                Customers cannot find categories reliably, mobile
                                layout breaks on several templates, and page weight
                                is high because of leftover scripts.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Strategy</h3>
                            <p>
                                Rebuild the information architecture before touching
                                visual design. Decide what the store sells, in what
                                groups, and how a first-time visitor reaches it in
                                two taps.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                    <div class="case-study-column">

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Implementation</h3>

                            <ul class="case-study-list">
                                <li>
                                    Audit collections and merge or retire overlapping ones
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Rebuild navigation around how customers shop,
                                    not how the catalogue is stored
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Rebuild key templates mobile-first on a clean,
                                    maintainable theme
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Remove unused apps and scripts, then re-check
                                    page weight
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>What this is designed to change</h3>

                            <ul class="case-study-list">
                                <li>
                                    A navigation a new visitor can use without instruction
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Consistent layout across every template on mobile
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    A lighter store that is cheaper and faster to maintain
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>
            </article>


            <!-- Store 03 -->
            <article class="case-study-card">
                <div class="case-study-meta">
                    <span class="case-study-meta-primary">Store 03</span>
                    <span>Focus: Klaviyo &amp; Email</span>
                    <span>Stage: Retention</span>
                </div>

                <h2 class="case-study-title">
                    All revenue comes from paid acquisition, none from the list
                </h2>

                <div class="case-study-grid">

                    <div class="case-study-column">

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Challenge</h3>
                            <p>
                                A store collects email addresses but sends only
                                occasional campaigns. Every sale has to be bought
                                again through ads.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Store situation</h3>
                            <p>
                                No welcome sequence, no abandoned checkout recovery,
                                no post-purchase follow-up, and a list that has
                                never been segmented.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Strategy</h3>
                            <p>
                                Install the flows that run without ongoing effort
                                first, because automated email earns while nothing
                                is being sent manually. Campaigns come after the
                                flows are live.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                    <div class="case-study-column">

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Implementation</h3>

                            <ul class="case-study-list">
                                <li>
                                    Welcome series for new subscribers with a clear
                                    first-purchase reason
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Abandoned checkout and browse abandonment recovery
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Post-purchase sequence covering delivery expectations,
                                    care and re-order
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Segment by purchase behaviour rather than sending
                                    everything to everyone
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>What this is designed to change</h3>

                            <ul class="case-study-list">
                                <li>
                                    Revenue that continues between campaigns
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Recovered checkouts that would otherwise have been lost
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Lower dependence on paid acquisition for repeat sales
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>
            </article>


            <!-- Store 04 -->
            <article class="case-study-card">
                <div class="case-study-meta">
                    <span class="case-study-meta-primary">Store 04</span>
                    <span>Focus: SEO Foundations</span>
                    <span>Stage: Organic growth</span>
                </div>

                <h2 class="case-study-title">
                    A store invisible to search because the basics were never set
                </h2>

                <div class="case-study-grid">

                    <div class="case-study-column">

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Challenge</h3>
                            <p>
                                A store ranks for its own brand name and nothing
                                else. Category and product pages are not being
                                found by people searching for what the store sells.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Store situation</h3>
                            <p>
                                Duplicate and templated meta titles, thin collection
                                pages, unstructured product descriptions, and no
                                internal linking between related products.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Strategy</h3>
                            <p>
                                Fix the technical and structural foundations before
                                producing content. Content added on a broken
                                foundation does not compound.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                    <div class="case-study-column">

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>Implementation</h3>

                            <ul class="case-study-list">
                                <li>
                                    Unique, intent-matched titles and descriptions
                                    across collections and products
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Collection pages given real, useful copy instead
                                    of a bare product grid
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Product structured data so listings display
                                    correctly in search results
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Internal linking between related products and
                                    their parent collections
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="case-study-block">
                            <h3>What this is designed to change</h3>

                            <ul class="case-study-list">
                                <li>
                                    Pages eligible to rank for what customers
                                    actually search for
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    Richer search listings that earn more clicks
                                    at the same position
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    A base that future content work can build on
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>
            </article>

        </div>

    </div>
</section>